# Turning a part of a mechanism (F9): the four-bar's coupler dragged by
# one of its lines with Ctrl held turns in the screen's plane, about
# the point, as far as its hinges let it: the crank and the rocker turn
# with it and the loop stays closed. One step of undo puts it back.
# Dragged with Shift, which turns it about the view's own axes, it
# turns by the share of that turn about the hinges' upright pins, the
# crank and the rocker with it. params prints the parts' placements.
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/fourbar.tlspr
menu File|Open...
params
down L 405 135
move 410 125 L ctrl
move 440 125 L ctrl
move 450 140 L ctrl
move 455 160 L ctrl
up L 455 160
params
key z ctrl
params
down L 405 135
move 410 125 L shift
move 420 115 L shift
move 430 105 L shift
up L 430 105
params
